-- Nov 10 Department WCM Hot Lab (Sean, 2026-11-10). Applied through ve-once-hotlab-1110 (now a 410 stub).

-- step: rulenotes
update public.bcps_audit_rule_reviews set updated_at=now(), comment = case check_id
when 'dense-content' then comment || ' Room (transcript): on first read the current wording did not make sense to enough people. Patricia Sapp: "is it run-on sentences, or dividing it up by subject?" Sean''s intent: content dropped in as story form, like a novel; instead a short topic sentence, supporting details as bullets, and accordions or tabs so it is not one glob of text. Option B (before and after) was also read; Patricia Sapp and Ernesto Gonzalez preferred A.'
when 'site-page-links' then comment || ' Room (transcript): Sean walked it live on the Academics page: right-click the link, Edit Link, and the dialog showed External Link, which is exactly the problem the rule flags. Sean: "I''ve seen this before, so I''m glad we''re finally getting an opportunity to address it." Ernesto Gonzalez seconded changing the wording to the External Link / Internal Link names.'
when 'quick-access' then 'Nov 10 Hot Lab: change. "Quick Access buttons" is not Sean''s term (it came from the June certification course, Module 2, not the District standards page); Patricia Sapp read it as the register / click-here buttons. Sean''s standard (transcript): a button is not the way to display your information. Each program or topic shows its information first, as regular visible text (aim for about 250 characters so people know what they are clicking through to), then a small button (not large) under it, left aligned. Text keeps the default style: no custom sizes or styles (add an audit check for altered text styles if one does not exist). Reason to give WCMs: not that our look is better, but consistency across departments, so your content is the differentiator, not the layout. Reviewed live: Early Childhood Education Head Start and volunteer sections are a good visual, but their program text has a different style applied that needs stripping. Rename and rewrite the rule (and the course page) around this standard; drop the 3 to 6 count. Pair it with a "See it done right" example once Sean picks the page.'
else comment end
where reviewer_email='contact@lesaruss.com' and check_id in ('dense-content','site-page-links','quick-access') and comment not like '%Room (transcript)%' and comment not like '%Sean''s standard (transcript)%';

