</div><p class="gap-note">Names from the Teams transcript. Others who joined without speaking are not listed.</p></div></details>
<details class="doc-accordion"><summary><h3>Audit Rules Reviewed</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">No long unbroken blocks of text</div><div class="point-detail">Change. New wording: "Break up long blocks of text."</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Every link has readable text</div><div class="point-detail">Change. Reworded to describe links with no text at all.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Internal links use site links, not copied addresses</div><div class="point-detail">Change. Steps now match Finalsite's link dialog: External Link, Internal Link, Resources.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">"Quick Access buttons"</div><div class="point-detail">Change. Renamed and rewritten around the button standard: information first, then a small left-aligned button.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Thirteen accessibility rules</div><div class="point-detail">Not a WCM's job. Moved to the Finalsite list.</div></div>
</div></details>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="g2" class="doc-group"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="g2">What We Decided</h2><p class="group-note">Decisions made in the meeting and questions still open.</p>
<details class="doc-accordion" open><summary><h3>Decisions</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>If a WCM cannot fix it in Composer, it goes to the Finalsite list.</strong> Thirteen rules moved, plus the Finalsite parts of two more.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Link instructions use Finalsite's own names.</strong> External Link, Internal Link, Resources, Media and Anchor, everywhere they are explained.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Buttons follow the information, they do not replace it.</strong> Regular text first, then a small button, left aligned, in the default text style.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Every rule shows what right looks like.</strong> A "See it done right" snapshot opens in a lightbox from the rule.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Layout is standard so content can stand out.</strong> Put your time into your content and media; ask the District Web Team for anything Finalsite cannot do.</div></div>
</div></details>
<details class="doc-accordion"><summary><h3>Open Questions</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Single-column layout</div><div class="point-detail">Next rule up. Can a WCM change the page layout themselves, and does single column apply to every page or only landing pages?</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Done-right example for buttons</div><div class="point-detail">Which department page becomes the example, under the new standard.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Jennifer Amador's page question</div><div class="point-detail">About a page that is not Early Childhood's. Not reached; first item Thursday.</div></div>
</div></details>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="g3" class="doc-group"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="g3">Your To-Do List</h2><p class="group-note">Who does what next.</p>
<details class="doc-accordion" open><summary><h3>Action Items</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">1</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Finish the audit rule review</div><div class="action-detail">About 15 rules left. Continue Thursday, November 12, and Monday; District Web Team reviews in between.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Sean A. Russell and the District Web Team</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">2</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Apply the decisions and rerun the audit</div><div class="action-detail">Reword the rules, move the Finalsite items off WCM lists, rerun every audit, then notify WCMs.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: District Web Team</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">3</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Fix the link instructions everywhere</div><div class="action-detail">Audit rule, WCM guide, certification course and related documents all use Finalsite's own link names.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: District Web Team</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">4</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Build "See it done right" examples</div><div class="action-detail">A snapshot of a correct page for each rule, opened in a lightbox.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: District Web Team</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">5</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Remove the old Hot Lab invite</div><div class="action-detail">So no one joins the wrong meeting room.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Sean A. Russell</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">6</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Send Early Childhood Education the instructions email</div><div class="action-detail">For the item built at the last session with Jennifer Amador's team.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Sean A. Russell</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">7</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Keep working your audit</div><div class="action-detail">The first review window ends December 18. Use Still stuck? on anything that does not make sense.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Department WCMs</div></div></div>
</div></details>
